description:
WARNING: This mod's values and balance implications should be adjusted to your own preference in Mod Settings before use.

Seize enemy ship control by hacking and boarding:
- Hacking Array (hull mod): locks onto an unmanned ship (Remnant automated ships / drones), hijacks it until control is taken; in Mod Settings you can enable hacking of Tesseract (Omega) ships and their faction (off by default, with an adjustable hack-speed multiplier); lower target CR and overloaded targets gain extra hack progress (on by default, tunable);
- Boarding Pod (fighter wing, Light / Medium / Heavy): accumulates boarding hits against manned ships until control is taken; in Mod Settings you can toggle boarding of phased targets (off by default) and all-shield (OMNI) targets (on by default); targets below a CR threshold gain a chance of an extra boarding hit every few seconds (on by default, tunable); successful boarding contacts consume marines from player cargo (Light 5 / Medium 10 / Heavy 20, on by default);
- Boarding Driver Core (hull mod): triggers electronic-interference malfunctions on the boarding side (engine / weapons / shield, including critical malfunctions);
- When a target is destroyed, one-shot boarding fighters are released according to its accumulated boarding count (set the sunk-return fraction to 0 to disable);
- Boarding/hack progress is shown as a colored arc around the target by default; you can turn it off in Mod Settings to restore progress floating-text;
- Add ship hull ids line by line to <mod root>/夺取黑名单.txt to blacklist them from hacking/boarding;
- Battle-end backstop: after the enemy has no surviving deployed ships for 10 seconds, the enemy fleet is ordered to retreat, preventing the battle from failing to end;
Captured ships join your fleet directly after the battle.

--- Author's Note ---
Thank you for downloading and playing. I am a complete coding novice - I did not write a single line of code for this mod (😂); it was entirely cobbled together by the AI (Doubao) referencing various other mods and vanilla code.
This is my first attempt to turn my ideas into a mod. If anything offends you, please forgive me - I am truly sorry!
